-- K7 of the audit of 2026-11-11 (docs/audit-2026-11-11.md), the rest after the hot tables (202611190100): every
-- foreign key in the public and private schemas gets an index that starts with its column. On 2026-11-21 a database
-- built from every migration of main (bf9acd6) had 206 such keys without one (193 in public, 13 in private), all of
-- a single column; most point to profiles (author, approver) and to reference tables (currencies, counterparties).
-- An index on the referencing column keeps deletes and key updates of the referenced row from scanning the whole
-- table and serves joins on it. Indexes only, no data changes; names <table>_<column>_idx.
-- Plain CREATE INDEX inside the migration transaction: the tables are small today. On large tables the owners may
-- prefer CREATE INDEX CONCURRENTLY outside a transaction instead.
